      "description": "Gemini Solar + Storage is an operating 690 MWac solar photovoltaic and 380 MW / approximately 1,416 MWh battery storage project in Clark County, Nevada, developed by Quinbrook with its portfolio company Primergy. The co-located facility supplies NV Energy under a 25-year power purchase agreement and is designed to meet approximately 10% of Nevada's peak power demand. APG acquired a 49% interest on behalf of ABP in 2022. In April 2024, Quinbrook's Valley of Fire Continuation Fund LP acquired the remaining 51%, and the project reached full commercial operations in 2024. A February 2026 refinancing continued to identify the same 51% Quinbrook / 49% APG ownership structure.",
